#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Common Biases in Behavioral Finance]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Overconfidence 😎]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("One of the most common biases in Behavioral Finance is overconfidence. This is when investors overestimate their abilities and the accuracy of their information.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Loss Aversion 📉]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Another common bias is loss aversion. This refers to the tendency for people to prefer avoiding losses to acquiring equivalent gains. In other words, the pain of losing is psychologically twice as powerful as the pleasure of gaining.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Herd Behavior 🐑]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("The third common bias is herd behavior. This is the tendency for individuals to mimic the actions of a larger group. Investors often follow the crowd, even if it means ignoring their own analysis.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Impact of Biases]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Lead to irrational decisions 🤔]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("These biases can lead investors to make irrational decisions. Overconfidence can cause investors to take on too much risk. Loss aversion can lead to holding on to losing investments for too long. And herd behavior can result in bubbles and crashes.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Affect market efficiency 📈]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("These irrational behaviors can affect market efficiency. If many investors are acting based on biases rather than rational analysis, prices can deviate from their fundamental values.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Mitigating Biases]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Awareness 🧠]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The first step in mitigating these biases is awareness. Investors need to be aware of their own psychological tendencies.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Education 📚]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Education can also help. Understanding how these biases work can help investors recognize them in their own behavior.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Systematic approach 📋]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Finally, investors can adopt a systematic approach to investing. By relying on objective criteria and a disciplined process, investors can minimize the impact of emotional biases on their decisions.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Summary]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Common biases: Overconfidence, Loss Aversion, Herd Behavior]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("In summary, the common biases in Behavioral Finance are overconfidence, loss aversion, and herd behavior.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Impact: Irrational decisions, Affect market efficiency]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("These biases can lead to irrational decisions and affect market efficiency.")
]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Mitigation: Awareness, Education, Systematic approach]
#only("3")[
